-- title:
--   Node places of the semistable fibre with charts and Hasse j-datum, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. For a prime $q$ and a nonzero level $M'$, $\mathcal F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to $H :=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (the units $\equiv 1 \bmod q$); `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` $= \mathbb Q\bigl(\,\mathrm{qExpand}_d\,j : d \mid M'\,\bigr)$; and for a field $k$, `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` is the subfield $k(j_q, j_{q,M'})$ of the Laurent series over $k$ generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k M'`, with distinguished element `jGeomGen k M'` $= j_q$.
--
--   **Data and hypothesis groups.** (A) *Residual supersingular datum.* A prime $q$ with $q = 2$; a level $M'$ with $M' \neq 0$ and $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit (`A.LiesOverPrime q`), with residue field $k := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` over $k$ which is exactly `ssPlaces q M' k`, the set of places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\,$`jGeomGen k M'`$\,) \in$ `ssJSet q k`; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into $\mathcal F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with target `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` lying over $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the reduction of $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places and the divisor-compatibility clause of the structure `ConstantReduction`); the hypothesis `hR₀` that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction, i.e. for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to k$; and a distinguished $s \in W$.
--
--   (B) *Small-field datum.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   (C) *Auxiliary prime and parameters.* A prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   (D) *Layer family.* A type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n \subseteq K_n$ defined by membership of $A$; an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$; and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in the image of some $K_n$.
--
--   (E) *Tame parameter.* An element $\pi_t \in A$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q$, and `htame`: every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise.
--
--   (F) *Base layer.* An intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b \subseteq K_b$ defined by membership of $A$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **The two universally quantified objects.** With $\mathcal F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb Q} \to \mathcal F$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \mathcal F$ satisfying (G) the *level-field conditions*: (G1) $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; (G2) the compositum of $F_0$ with $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ inside $\mathcal F$ is all of $\mathcal F$; (G3) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (G4) linear disjointness: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every finite family $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the image of $K'$ and every family $c_i \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$;
--
--   and for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying (H), the *descended model datum with nodes, node charts, Drinfeld quotient and Igusa separation*, whose clauses are: (H1) $W_0$ lies over $A \cap k_0$ ($x \in A \iff$ the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$, for $x \in k_0$); (H2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; (H3) $\pi_0$ generates its maximal ideal; (H4) the specialisation clause at $s$: for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, if $g$ is regular wherever $j_q$ is (at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, $0 \le \mathrm{ord}_P(j_q)$ implies $0 \le \mathrm{ord}_P(g)$) and the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $k$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; (H5) $W_0$ is stable under the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that $f \in W_0 \iff$ its image lies in $W_0$ whenever both lie in $F_0$; (H6) the existence of an affine chart: a subring $B$ of $\mathcal F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q} \to \mathcal F$, such that $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the image of $K_b$ and that compositum is the set of fractions $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $f \in W_0$ exactly for the fractions $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the image of $j_q$ lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b$ of $B \cap F_0$ vanishing on no valuation subring of $F_0$ over $A \cap k_0$ at which $\pi_0$ is a nonunit and $j_q$ is integral over $A \cap k_0$ (more precisely, $b \notin V$ for all such $V$); for each $s' \in W$ with $s' \neq s$ there is an element $b$ of $B \cap F_0$ with $b \notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ over $A \cap k_0$ satisfying the specialisation clause (H4) with $s'$ in place of $s$; a Drinfeld clause: for every $(\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2)$-algebra structure on $k$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q k Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the $C_s$-translations) with $|C_s| =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, kernel the ideal generated by $\varpi_b$, reduction-compatibility on $A_b$, the property that every element of the target is a fraction of values of $\rho$, the characterisation of the image of $\rho$ as the elements coming from `CoordRing q k`, and equivariance: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$, $\rho$ of that element is the image of $\rho(f)$ under [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16); and finally the node clause: $j_q$ lies in `R₀.integers` with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, `jqNModC` $\bar{\mathbb Q}\,q$ lies in $\mathcal F$, there is $a_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ with $(\mathrm{res}_A a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, and there is a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with $q+1$ elements which are all localisations of one finitely generated subring $B_c =$ closure of (the image of $k_0 \cap A$) together with a finite set, which is permuted transitively by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, whose members are pairwise separated by elements that are units in one and nonunits in another, such that each valuation subring of $F_0$ over $A \cap k_0$ satisfying (H4) either contains $B$ or dominates one of the nodes, and such that each node $\mathcal O$ is contained in $W_0$, is local and Noetherian, lies over $A \cap k_0$ with residue field generated by $k_0 \cap A$, and carries a crossing presentation: an exponent $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{pwc}(s)}v$ for a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$, where $\mathrm{pwc}(s) =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` $=$ `jWidthChar q` of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` (for $q = 2$ the numerator is $12$ at $j = 0$ and $1$ otherwise), elements $c_x, c_y \in \mathcal O$ and a unit $u$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the completion of $\mathcal O$ at its maximal ideal with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the completion of $A \cap k_0$ at modulus $\pi_0^{E_0}$ carrying $k_0 \cap A$ to constants and $c_x, c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$, $V$, with $c_y$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and $c_x$ outside it, a Hasse datum expressing `jqNModC`$\,-\,a_0$ as a unit times $V^e$ with $e \ge 1$, an auxiliary discrete valuation ring $W_x \supseteq \mathcal O$ of $F_0$ over $A \cap k_0$ uniformised by $\pi_0$ with a residually transcendental element, at which $c_x$ is a nonunit and $c_y$ a unit, which computes the vanishing of $R_0$-residues and detects $\mathcal O$ on the specialisation clause at $s$, and which separates $\mathcal O$ from the other nodes (for $\mathcal O' \neq \mathcal O$ there is $f \in \mathcal O'$ with $f \notin W_x$), and a finitely generated subring $B_x \subseteq B \cap \mathcal O$ consisting of functions regular wherever $j_q$ is, with $\mathcal O$ its localisation, $F_0$ its fraction field, $B_x$ the closure of the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, and an element of $B_x$ that lies outside every valuation subring of $F_0$ over $A \cap k_0$ with $\pi_0$ a nonunit, $j_q$ integral, and not containing all of $\mathcal O$. (The clauses of (H6) are as listed; all of them are assumed.)
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under (A)–(H), for every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ which is a $k$-algebra and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathcal F$ with residue field target $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $\mathcal F$ over $A$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathrm{FSS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the reduction of $A$, and with the scaling property of `RegularProlongation`), assumed compatible with $W_0$ in the sense that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in$ `R.integers` $\iff f \in W_0$, there exists a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $k$ with $|N| = q+1$, and there exist: a family of fields $\mathrm{FI}_x$ indexed by the places $x$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $k$, each a $k$-algebra; regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ to $\mathcal F$ with targets $\mathrm{FI}_x$; places $b_x$ of $\mathrm{FI}_x$ over $k$; subrings $C'_l \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$; complete discrete valuation rings $\mathrm{Wc}_l$ with elements $\pi_l$, exponents $E_l \in \mathbb N$ and an exponent $E_0 \in \mathbb N$; sets $S(\mathrm{nd})$ of places of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; subrings $\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ and $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ of $\mathcal F$, the latter local and Noetherian; and elements $c_x(\mathrm{nd}), c_y(\mathrm{nd}), c_u(\mathrm{nd})$ of $\mathcal F$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) For each $n$ and $c \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$: $c \in C'_n$ if and only if $c \in A$ and $c$ lies in the image of $K_n$; (2) for each $l$ and $d \in C'_l$, the reduction of $d$ in $k$ vanishes if and only if $\varpi'_l \mid d$ in $C'_l$; (3) $C'_{n_0} \le C'_l$ for all $l$; (4) $\varpi'_{n_0} \neq 0$; (5) every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; (6) each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and each $E_l \ge 1$; (7) every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with trivial tame character relative to $\pi_t$ fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; (8) there are $w \ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0} = v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$ in $A$.
--
--   (9) For each $\mathrm{nd} \in N$: the places $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$, $\mathrm{nd}$ and all $P \in S(\mathrm{nd})$ are rational; $\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ consists exactly of those $f$ lying in `(Rx nd).integers`, in `R.integers` and in the valuation subring of every $P \in S(\mathrm{nd})$; for $f \in \mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ and $P \in S(\mathrm{nd})$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$; $c_x(\mathrm{nd})\,c_y(\mathrm{nd}) = (\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}c_u(\mathrm{nd})$; the $R_x$-residue of $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ vanishes, the order at $\mathrm{nd}$ of the $R$-residue of $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ is $1$, the $R$-residue of $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$ vanishes, and the order at $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$ of the $R_x$-residue of $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$ is $1$ (each clause conditional on the relevant integrality); for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with trivial tame character relative to $\pi_t$, the semilinear automorphism $g$ of $\mathcal F$ given by [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) applied to $\tau$ (coefficientwise action of $\tau$) preserves $S(\mathrm{nd})$ and fixes $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ and $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$; every $f \in \mathcal F$ is a fraction $a/b$ with $a, b \in \mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ for some $l$, $b \neq 0$; every $f \in \mathcal F$ satisfies $f b = \sum_i c_i a_i$ for some $b \neq 0$ and $a_i$ in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, n_0)$ and $c_i \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$; and for every $l$: $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, n_0) \le \mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l) \le \mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$; $S(\mathrm{nd})$ is exactly the set of places of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ dominating $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ (containing it in their valuation subring and sending its nonunits into the maximal ideal of $A$); the image of $C'_l$ lies in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$; every element of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ is congruent to an element of $C'_l$ modulo nonunits; families from $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ satisfy no relation with $C'_l$-linearly independent coefficients from $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; there is a subring $B_x \subseteq \mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ containing $c_x(\mathrm{nd}), c_y(\mathrm{nd}), c_u(\mathrm{nd})$ with $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ its localisation and $B_x$ the closure of the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ and $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$ lie in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ and $c_u(\mathrm{nd})$ is a unit there; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $\mathrm{Wc}_l$ to the completion of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ at its maximal ideal and an isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ E l)` such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c \circ \sigma$ is the constant embedding, every element of $C'_l$ with image in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ is $\sigma$ of some element of $\mathrm{Wc}_l$, and the two branch clauses hold: if $f \in \mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd}, l)$ has nonzero $R_x$-residue of order $n$ at $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$ then $\iota_c(f) - \gamma V^n$ lies in the ideal generated by the constant $\pi_l$ and $U$ for some unit $\gamma$ of the crossing model, and symmetrically with $U$ and $V$ interchanged for nonzero $R$-residue of order $n$ at $\mathrm{nd}$.
--
--   (10) Distinct members of $N$ have disjoint sets $S$. (11) For $\mathrm{nd} \in N$, $P \in S(\mathrm{nd})$, and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` regular wherever $j_q$ is, with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and $a \in A$ whose reduction equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue: $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ is congruent to $a$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. (12) For each $\zeta' \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ carrying $N$ into $N$ with $(\,$`levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ`$) \cdot P \in S(\mathrm{nd}) \iff P \in S(\tau_N \mathrm{nd})$ and with the pullback of `(Rx nd).integers` along that automorphism equal to `(Rx (τN nd)).integers`. (13) For every $\tau$ in the subgroup of automorphisms of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves `R.integers`, the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut` moves $N$ into $N$ and transports the sets $S$ accordingly ($\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(S(\mathrm{nd})) = S(\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot \mathrm{nd})$). (14) For $\mathrm{nd} \in N$, the image in $\mathcal F$ of any element of `R₀.integers` lies in `(Rx nd).integers`. (15) For each $\mathrm{nd} \in N$ there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` to $\mathrm{FI}_{\mathrm{nd}}$ which identifies $R_0$-residues with $R_x$-residues and which pulls the valuation subring of $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$ back to that of $s$.
--
--   (16) Hasse datum at $j$: `jqNModC` $\bar{\mathbb Q}\,q$ lies in $\mathcal F$, and there is $a_0 \in A$ such that this element minus $a_0$ lies in `R.integers` with vanishing $R$-residue, the $q$-th power of the reduction of $a_0$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen k M'`, and there is $c' \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ such that $c'$ times that difference lies in `R.integers` with nonzero residue and, for every $\mathrm{nd} \in N$, the difference lies in `(Rx nd).integers` with nonzero $R_x$-residue and $\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{nd}}$ of the $R$-residue of the scaled difference equals minus $\mathrm{ord}_{b_x(\mathrm{nd})}$ of that $R_x$-residue.
--
--   (17) For $x \in N$ and any place $y \notin N$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ there is $g \in$ `R.integers` lying in $\mathcal N_0(x, n_0)$, a nonunit there, whose $R$-residue is nonzero of order $0$ at $y$, and which lies in the valuation subring of every rational place of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j_q$ is regular. (18) For distinct $x, x' \in N$ there is $g$ lying in $\mathcal N_0(x, n_0)$ and in $\mathcal N_0(x', n_0)$ which is $c_x(x)$ times a unit in the former and a unit in the latter.
--
--   (19) Covering: every rational place $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying the specialisation condition at $s$ (for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` regular wherever $j_q$ is, with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a \in A$ whose reduction equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ is congruent to $a$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$) either belongs to $S(\mathrm{nd})$ for some $\mathrm{nd} \in N$, or lies in a residue disc of $R$ centred at a place $Q \notin N$: there are $Q \notin N$, a set $D$ of places of $\mathcal F$ and $z \in \mathcal F$ with `R.IsResidueDisc Q D z` (the conjunction of the disc-coordinate, pointwise-reduction and degree conditions) and $P \in D$.
--
--   This is the case $q = 2$, at a rigid auxiliary level ($\ell_g \equiv 11 \bmod 12$ dividing $M'$), of the passage from a descended model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over $A \cap k_0$ — an affine chart, the $q+1$ node local rings with their crossing presentations, node charts, Drinfeld quotient and Igusa-branch separation — to the corresponding data on the special fibre of an arbitrary regular prolongation $R$: the finite set $N$ of $q+1$ node places, their branch prolongations $R_x$, the attached sets $S(\mathrm{nd})$ of places of the generic fibre, the layerwise crossing models, the Hasse datum on $j$, and the statement that the rational points specialising to the supersingular point $s$ are covered by the node clusters together with residue discs. It feeds the one-existential constructor [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart), which assembles the semistable model of $X_H$ at $q = 2$ used in the level-lowering step.
